        "procedure": "Under Ar, triethylamine (98 µL, 0.67 mmol, 2.3 equiv) was added to HL·HCl (100 mg, 1 equiv) in CH3CN (3 mL). A CH3CN solution of La(ClO4)3·xH2O (x = 2–4, 0.44 equiv) was dropped in, and the mixture was stirred 4–5 h. The solvent was evaporated and the raw solid dried under high vacuum. La, Gd, and Tb complexes could not be isolated salt-free because of high MeOH solubility; analyses were performed on the raw solids.",
